# Vercel CLI's local-directory deploy is supposed to fall back to .gitignore
# when no .vercelignore exists, but the last `vercel --prod` upload hit
# Vercel's 100MB single-file limit at 1.4GB total — meaning something git
# ignores was still going into the deploy payload. Rather than depend on that
# fallback behaving identically to git's own ignore matching, this repeats
# the entries that must never leave this machine, explicitly, for Vercel.

# ~515MB of untouched 4K source PNGs — Drive is the source of truth for these,
# and public/assets/round8-web (the deployable optimized WebP output of
# `npm run assets:round8`) is what the site actually serves. This was the
# confirmed cause of the oversized upload.
/public/assets/round8/

/node_modules
/.next/
/.next-playwright-mock/
/out/
/build
/coverage
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/playwright/.cache/
.git

# scripts/qa-handover-capture.mjs output — generated screenshots, not source
/qa-handover-output/
